# The order the relay line keeps between its releases (docs/releases.md, Order between relay
# releases), read by `ci/release.sh relay tag` and `ci/release.sh relay order`. One entry per line,
# blank lines and lines starting with # ignored:
#
#   relay URL      a relay whose GET /v0/version says what it serves; a release that must wait for
#                  an earlier one waits for every relay named here
#   served X.Y.Z   every relay named here serves this relay release or a newer one. What a release up
#                  to this one carries is live, so no relay is asked about it
#   needs COMMIT   the full id of a commit of main every relay must serve before any release holding
#                  this line is tagged. A change that depends on an earlier one being live on the
#                  relays adds its line in its own pull request, with why after the id
#
# Adding a `needs` line, raise `served` to what the relays serve and drop the lines it answers. This
# file is in no release path, so an edit alone cuts no release.

relay https://dinners.digestif.io
relay https://dinners.rcherkasov.workers.dev
served 0.1.76
